node_modules/
# shanauto.db* also covers its -wal, -shm and hand-taken .bak- copies.
data/shanauto.db*
# Any OTHER sqlite file under data/ too. An empty stray data/ledger.db sat
# untracked for a day because only shanauto.db* was listed.
data/*.db
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
data/browser-profile/
data/artifacts/
data/runs/
# Written continuously mid-run; tracking it would fight ensureClean.
data/journal/
state/KILLSWITCH
state/run.lock
# Orchestrator-owned handoff briefs written into a worker repo (§9.4). The
# real defence is diffStat excluding .shanauto/ from every measurement; this
# stops the briefs riding into an owner's own `git add -A` if a repo this
# orchestrator manages is the orchestrator's own.
.shanauto/
.env
*.log

# From-zero run directories. Each is a complete throwaway instance — its own
# ledger, reports, journal and agent artifacts — created by pointing
# SHANAUTO_DB at it to reproduce the whole pipeline from an empty database.
# Twenty-four of them came to 22MB. The findings they produced live in
# docs/DECISIONS.md; the runs themselves are scratch.
.zero*/

# Generated by hand from a run's data, not source.
shanauto-deep-audit-report.html

# Written by a rollback so the stashes it took can be traced back to a run.
# Scratch: the stash itself is the artifact, and `git stash list` is the index.
data/rollback-stash-manifest-*.txt

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ privacy
# Everything below names the operator's own projects, paths and ideas. None of
# it is source, and all of it describes private repositories by name, absolute
# path, commit SHA and file. Tracked by accident until 2026-10-05.

# The allowlist: absolute paths to your projects on your disk. config/
# repos.yaml.example is the tracked one; copy it to config/repos.yaml.
config/repos.yaml

# Durable memory: example-api/example-ledger commit SHAs, paths, symbols and task
# reasons. NOT scratch -- the brain reads these for context, and `sa prune`
# refuses to touch them. Ignored, never deleted.
data/memory/

# Daily and weekly reports: every repo, task title and path the run touched.
data/reports/

# The ideas you typed, verbatim, once the planner has shaped them.
ideas/archive/

# A stray empty sqlite file. `data/*.db` was listed and `state/` was not.
state/*.db
